# Angular 22 Rules

The frontend (`apps/web/`) targets **Angular 22** and runs **zoneless**
(`provideZonelessChangeDetection()`, no `zone.js`).

## Angular 22 defaults — do not re-add removed boilerplate

| Concern | Angular ≤ 21 | Angular 22 (this project) |
|---|---|---|
| `standalone: true` | required flag | **default — omit it** |
| `changeDetection` | `Default` (eager) | **`OnPush` is the default**; we still declare it explicitly (see `performance.mdc`) |
| `provideHttpClient(withFetch())` | opt-in fetch backend | **fetch is the default — drop `withFetch()`** |
| Async data | `HttpClient` + `subscribe` | **`httpResource()` for GET**, `HttpClient` for mutations |
| Forms | Reactive / template-driven | **Signal Forms** (`@angular/forms/signals`) where validation/state matters |

These APIs (`httpResource`, `resource`, `rxResource`, Signal Forms) are **stable**
since v22 — no experimental imports or flags.

## Components

Standalone components only, never `NgModule`. Since Angular 19+ standalone is the
default, so **omit the redundant `standalone: true`** flag (it is implied):

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT – standalone is the default, no explicit flag needed
@Component({
  selector: 'app-version-card',
  imports: [FormsModule],
  templateUrl: './version-card.component.html',
  styleUrl: './version-card.component.scss',
})
export class VersionCardComponent {}

// ❌ WRONG – redundant standalone: true
@Component({ selector: 'app-version-card', standalone: true, /* ... */ })

// ❌ WRONG – no NgModule
@NgModule({ declarations: [VersionCardComponent] })
```

## Signals (signal-first state)

```typescript
// State as Signals
readonly versions = signal<InstalledNodeVersion[]>([]);
readonly isLoading = signal(false);
readonly errorMessage = signal<string | null>(null);

// Computed values
readonly hasVersions = computed(() => this.versions().length > 0);

// linkedSignal: writable state derived from another signal
readonly versionInput = linkedSignal(() => this.prefillVersion());
```

Use the **signal-based primitives**, not the legacy decorators:

- `input()` / `input.required()` instead of `@Input()`
- `output()` instead of `@Output()` / `EventEmitter`
- `model()` for two-way bindings, `viewChild()` / `contentChild()` for queries
- `inject()` instead of constructor DI

## Data fetching — `httpResource` for reads, `HttpClient` for writes

Read-only endpoints are fetched declaratively with **`httpResource`** (stable in
v22). It keeps the async state (`value` / `isLoading` / `error`) inside the signal
graph — no manual subscription, no `ngOnInit`:

```typescript
import { httpResource } from '@angular/common/http';

// GET resource — auto-loads, reactive, reloadable via .reload()
private readonly installed = httpResource<InstalledVersionsResponse>(
  () => '/api/versions/installed',
);
readonly versions = computed(() =>
  this.installed.hasValue() ? (this.installed.value()?.versions ?? []) : [],
);

// Lazy: return undefined from the URL factory until a trigger flips
private readonly remote = httpResource<RemoteVersionsResponse>(
  () => (this.shouldLoad() ? '/api/versions/remote' : undefined),
);
```

Imperative **mutations** (POST/DELETE: install, use, uninstall, alias edits)
stay on a thin typed `HttpClient` service (`nvm-api.service.ts`):

```typescript
private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);

installVersion(version: string): Observable<NvmCommandResult> {
  return this.http.post<NvmCommandResult>(`${this.baseUrl}/versions/install`, { version });
}
```

HTTP errors are normalised to `Error` once, globally, by `httpErrorInterceptor`
(`provideHttpClient(withInterceptors([httpErrorInterceptor]))`) — components/services
do not need their own `catchError`. Surface a resource's failure via its `error()`
signal (e.g. log it in an `effect`); never swallow it.

## Signal Forms (`@angular/forms/signals`)

For inputs that need validation or form state, prefer **Signal Forms** over
`FormsModule`/`ngModel` and Reactive Forms:

```typescript
import { form, FormField, required, pattern } from '@angular/forms/signals';

// In @Component({ imports: [FormField] })
readonly version = signal('22');
readonly versionForm = form(this.version, (f) => {
  required(f, { message: 'Bitte eine Version angeben.' });
  pattern(f, /^(node|stable|lts\/\*|\d+(\.\d+){0,2})$/, { message: 'Ungültiges Format.' });
});
```

```html
<input [formField]="versionForm" />
@let field = versionForm();
@if (field.touched() && field.invalid()) {
  <span role="alert">@for (e of field.errors(); track e.kind) { {{ e.message }} }</span>
}
<button [disabled]="field.invalid()">Installieren</button>
```

Mirror backend validators (e.g. the version `VERSION_PATTERN`) client-side for
instant feedback — the backend still validates independently (defence in depth).

## SCSS

- Variables in `_variables.scss`, no magic numbers in components
- BEM naming convention for classes (`.card__title`, `.card--active`)
- No external UI libraries (own SCSS only)
- Mobile-first, but primarily desktop-focused for this local tool

## Template Rules

- `@if` / `@for` / `@switch` and `@let` instead of `*ngIf` / `*ngFor` (built-in control flow)
- No inline styles in templates
- Disable buttons during active operations with `[disabled]="isLoading()"`
  (or, for Signal Forms, `[disabled]="form().invalid()"`)

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)

- Every `<button>` needs an accessible name: visible text or `[attr.aria-label]`
- Row-level buttons must include context in `aria-label` (e.g. `'Version ' + v.version + ' verwenden'`)
- Decorative SVGs: `aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"`
- Tables: `scope="col"` on all `<th>`, `aria-label` or `<caption>` on `<table>`, `[attr.aria-current]="v.active ? 'true' : null"` on active row
- Dynamic content (loading/results/errors): wrap in `aria-live` region or use Angular CDK `LiveAnnouncer`
- Modals: `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, `cdkTrapFocus`, focus restore on close, `@HostListener('keydown.escape')` to close
- No `tabindex > 0`; never remove focus ring without a visible alternative
- For detailed patterns and per-component checklist, use the `a11y-expert` skill
